# Cloudflare Pages quirks this file has to live with (doc/redirects_en.md):
#   - Pages resolves /x to /x.html and 308s /x/ to /x before reading this file,
#     so rules that just restate those two behaviours never fire.
#   - Pages rejects the "200!" suffix as an invalid status code.
#   - A wildcard rule whose target is "/index.html" is dropped in silence.
#     Pages exposes the root document as "/", so that target never resolves.
#     Rewrites must target "/" — this is what silently ate the SPA fallback.
#   - Rules match top-down, so the SPA prefix block has to stay last.
# Retired-URL 301s do NOT live here: Pages caps this file, so that family is
# owned by the Worker (backend/api/worker/src/legacyRedirects.generated.ts,
# mirrored from dist/data/legacy-redirects.json by
# front/scripts/sync_redirects_to_worker.mjs). Keep this file tiny.
# Guard: npm run check:redirects.

/api/* https://store.balancebiketoddler.com/api/:splat 307

# Bare app roots have no prerendered sibling, so the shell needs an explicit
# rewrite. Their sub-paths are covered by the SPA prefix block below.
/compare / 200
/auth / 200
/search / 200
/evaluations / 200
/transparency / 200

# SPA fallback: keep last. Never widen it to a global catch-all: that answers
# every unknown path (inbound spam under .php suffixes included) with the
# homepage shell and a 200, and Pages has no 404 rewrite to compensate.
/products/* / 200
/reviews/* / 200
/evaluations/* / 200
/guides/* / 200
/news/* / 200
/transparency/* / 200
/about/* / 200
/compare/* / 200
/auth/* / 200
/search/* / 200
